  "enhanced_information": "Chemotherapy primarily targets rapidly dividing cells, which explains why certain organs and cell types are more susceptible to its effects. Cardiac myocytes have a very low turnover rate, making them relatively resistant to chemotherapy. In contrast, enterocytes and hematopoietic cells have high turnover rates, rendering them more susceptible to chemotherapeutic agents. Hair follicle cells also divide rapidly and are therefore susceptible. Liver hepatocytes possess a unique regenerative capacity, allowing them to tolerate some chemotherapy effects, but they can still be affected. Thus, among the options provided, cardiac myocytes are the most resistant to chemotherapeutic agents due to their low proliferation rate."
